@code_type gdscript .gd
@comment_type # %s

@s main

- make a pong node as root scene
- 750x750 or web

@s Ball
- root, area2d
    - collision shape
    - sprite

--- ball.gd
extends Area2D

const DEFAULT_SPEED = 100
var _speed = DEFAULT_SPEED
var direction = Vector2.LEFT # go to the left at the start
@onready var _initial_pos = position

func _process(delta):
	_speed += delta * 2
	position += _speed * delta * direction


func reset():
	# direction = Vector2.LEFT
	direction = Vector2(direction.x,0) # loser starts
	# direction = Vector2(-direction.x,0) # winner starts
	position = _initial_pos
	_speed = DEFAULT_SPEED
---

We have a ball, so now let's add paddles

@s Paddle

--- paddle.gd
extends Area2D

const MOVE_SPEED = 100

var _ball_dir
var _up
var _down

@onready var _screen_size_y = get_viewport_rect().size.y # allows for responsive (web term) upper/lower bounds

func _ready():
    # as there are 2 paddles being controlled by the same code
    # name = the name you give the node in the node tree
	var n = String(name).to_lower()
	_up = n + "_move_up"
	_down = n + "_move_down"
	if n == "left":
		_ball_dir = 1
	else:
		_ball_dir = -1


func _process(delta):
	# Move up and down based on input.
	var input = Input.get_action_strength(_down) - Input.get_action_strength(_up) # todo
	position.y = clamp(position.y + input * MOVE_SPEED * delta, 16, _screen_size_y - 16) # force number to be between 2 values, in this case, 0 < where pos.y will be < screen_size (also account for paddle width is where the 16 comes from)


func _on_area_entered(area):
	if area.name == "Ball":
		# Assign new direction.
		area.direction = Vector2(_ball_dir, randf() * 2 - 1).normalized()

---

- set inputs
`left_move_down`
`left_move_up`
`right_move_down`
`right_move_up`

- signals
- connect on_area_entered emitted from left to itself

@s walls
Walls are just area2ds with colshapes

--- wall.gd
extends Area2D

func _on_wall_area_entered(area):
	if area.name == "Ball":
		#oops, ball went out of game place, reset
		area.reset()
---

connect signal to itself

@s floor and ceiling
similar code to wall but instead of reseting we bounce the ball

--- ceiling_floor.gd
extends Area2D

@export var _bounce_direction = 1

func _on_area_entered(area):
	if area.name == "Ball":
		area.direction = (area.direction + Vector2(0, _bounce_direction)).normalized()
---

set bounce direction to be -1 for floor in export vars

- export to web with the export, get a mirror sorted and local host (python)
